spoint veg+rocks PERF architecture (built on dna-quality-fixes, commits a3500332..59864b38, follows the veg-rocks-planet-run fixes). (1) ROCKS = ONE three.BatchedMesh (native, three 0.183) holding all 6 SDF rock geometries -> a SINGLE multiDraw call (was 6x InstancedMesh2). client/core/Rocks.js: addGeometry per type once, addInstance(gid)+setMatrixAt+setColorAt per placement, deleteInstance on unload; native perObjectFrustumCulled+sortObjects default true; per-instance shade via setColorAt (NOT a custom uniform); procedural object-local rock texture (multi-octave value noise, no UVs/asset/CORS) preserved; rockDrawCalls=1 witnessed. NO per-instance mesh-LOD (rocks res-16 low-poly, the draw-merge is the win). bm.frustumCulled=false (it does its own per-instance cull). @three.ez/batched-mesh-extensions NOT needed (native BatchedMesh suffices); vp-batched-mesh-dep can stay deferred. (2) VEG draw-call metric: window.__vegProfile.vegDrawCalls = sum of active-LOD render groups across branch+leaf (real veg cost), vs the misleading whole-scene renderer.info.drawCalls. (3) front-to-back SORT: all veg branch+leaf InstancedMesh2 + rocks set sortObjects=true + customSort=createRadixSort(im) (early-Z overdraw cut; import createRadixSort from @three.ez/instanced-mesh). (4) BIOME distribution: VegPlacement.baseDensity(temp,humidity,erosion=0) thins forest up to 45% in eroded ground (the SAME anchorField erosion that makes rocks denser) -> trees+rocks anti-correlate into rocky-vs-forested biomes; erosion default 0 keeps the 2-arg test contract; classify passes clim.erosion. (5) PLACEMENT cost: RockPlacement.classify now does the sea/climate reject BEFORE the 4 slope groundHeightLocal samples (mirrors the existing VegPlacement coin-before-slope reorder) -> ocean cells pay 1 sample not 5 (witnessed 16 vs 80 calls/chunk); land cells still 5 (rock density depends on slopeRatio). Parity-safe (sea reject non-rand). (6) SPATIAL packing already correct: @three.ez InstancedMesh2 partial-inserts streamed instances into the BVH (Instances.js:103 this.bvh?.insert(id) via onCreation), BVH built ONCE (bvhBuilt guard), margin 8, branch+leaf share ONE full-tree boundingSphere. (7) FALLBACK fix: Vegetation loadChunk looks up the species record by NAME (recByName Map), not array index -> a failed species build no longer mis-maps every later species (the array compacts on push-on-success). REMAINING heavy roadmap (untouched): vp-drawcall-merge (veg bark+leaf atlas->single material, large), vp-shared-impostor-atlas/vp-impostor-tier-shared-atlas (cross-species sampler2DArray, the documented #1 GPU win, large), vp-30k-144-witness-HARD (needs the atlas first), ff-grass-system (new content), vp-tv8-terrain-perf/vp-streaming-gltf-perf (cross-repo), ff research workflows.